ZGeo change log
===============

Version 1.27.0 — 2026-11-13
Previous GitHub release: v1.26.1 (2026-11-12)

Overview
--------
ZGeo 1.27.0 adds an optional "Metadata and CRS" check.

Changes in 1.27.0
-----------------
- Added the "Metadata and CRS" check:
  - SHP: missing `.prj` and `.cpg`;
  - rasters: missing `.aux.xml` and `.ovr`;
  - rasters without a CRS: missing `.tfw`, `.tifw` or `.wld` world file;
  - deprecated CRS;
  - CRS without an EPSG/authority code;
  - non-metric units for projected CRS;
  - non-degree units for geographic CRS;
  - non-standard axis order for projected CRS.
- The check is optional and disabled by default.
- The checks window now shows 8 checks when JSON files are present.
- README, metadata, translations and tests were updated.

Available checks in 1.27.0
--------------------------
Refinement:
- Refine size (all formats, including SHP and MIF/MID)
- Refine CRS and check it
- Refine feature count and check empty layers

Validation:
- Check JSON for GeoJSON format
- Field name check
- Dataset integrity check
- Metadata and CRS check
- Geometry and coordinate check

Excel export sheets
-------------------
- "Files" — the filtered file list;
- "Statistics" — statistics by format;
- one sheet per problem check with issues;
- "Check statistics" — totals by check.

Compatibility
-------------
- QGIS 3.16 and newer, including QGIS 4 / Qt 6.
- Python 3.9+.
- Windows is the primary target; the plugin uses QGIS and PyQt APIs.

Installation
------------
1. Download `zgeo-1.27.0.zip`.
2. In QGIS open Plugins → Manage and Install Plugins → Install from ZIP.
3. Select the downloaded archive and restart QGIS if it was running.

